implementationPlan.description:
In scripts/local-runner/dependency-cache.mjs only, make admitEntries refuse every lockfile field npm ci trusts that admission skipped. Error handling stays the module's own: one fixed code per refusal kind through dependencyError; no message carries a spec, path, URL or lockfile byte; the refusal comes before any fetch or mkdir; admitLockfiles stays pure and never returns a partial result.

1. After isRecord/hasExactKeys (they are consts, so not above them), add:
```js
// The dependency maps npm ci builds an entry's edges from, and the specs npm-package-arg resolves only from the registry
// or refuses: an npm: alias, whose target it requires to be a registry spec, or a version, range or tag. Those hold no
// ':', '/', '\\', '@', '#' or '%', start with no '.' and end in no tarball suffix, which it reads as a URL, git or a path.
const DEPENDENCY_MAPS = ['dependencies', 'devDependencies', 'optionalDependencies', 'peerDependencies'];
const RANGE_OR_TAG = /^(?!\.)[\w !'()*+.<=>^|~-]*$/;
const TARBALL = /[.](?:tgz|tar\.gz|tar)$/i;
const registrySpec = spec => typeof spec === 'string' && (spec.startsWith('npm:') || (RANGE_OR_TAG.test(spec) && !TARBALL.test(spec)));
const registrySpecs = entry => DEPENDENCY_MAPS.every(key => entry[key] === undefined
  || (isRecord(entry[key]) && Object.values(entry[key]).every(registrySpec)));
```
2. In admitEntries' loop, replace the root skip and the inBundle skip:
```js
    const location = key === '' ? null : LOCATION.exec(key);
    if (key !== '' && location === null) throw dependencyError('DEPENDENCY_LOCATION_INVALID');
    if (!isRecord(entry)) throw dependencyError('DEPENDENCY_LOCKFILE_INVALID');
    // The root's edges too: npm ci re-resolves an edge its locked node does not satisfy from that edge's spec.
    if (!registrySpecs(entry)) throw dependencyError('DEPENDENCY_SOURCE_UNSUPPORTED');
    if (key === '') continue;
    // (the existing link comment and `entry.link === true` refusal stay here, unchanged)
    // npm installs what a truthy hasShrinkwrap or legacy _hasShrinkwrap entry's own npm-shrinkwrap.json names.
    if (entry.hasShrinkwrap || entry._hasShrinkwrap) throw dependencyError('DEPENDENCY_SOURCE_UNSUPPORTED');
    // npm fetches a bundled entry from its own resolved (or legacy _resolved) when the root bundles it or its bundler's
    // tarball lacks it, so only one naming neither ships solely inside a verified tarball.
    if (entry.inBundle === true) {
      if (entry.resolved !== undefined || entry._resolved !== undefined) throw dependencyError('DEPENDENCY_SOURCE_UNSUPPORTED');
      continue;
    }
```
The platform-skip line and everything after it stay unchanged. The order matters and is tested: specs before the root continue, shrinkwrap before both skips, the bundled check before the optional skip. Truthiness for the shrinkwrap flags mirrors npm, whose Node takes hasShrinkwrap || pkg._hasShrinkwrap. Keep `=== true` for inBundle, optional and link: a truthy non-true value there already gets the stricter registry checks.
3. Update the header's Rules list. Every entry, the root included, is an object whose four maps hold only registry specs (npm re-resolves unmet edges from their specs). No entry is shrinkwrapped (npm installs what the tarball's own shrinkwrap names). A bundled entry is skipped only when it names no resolved or _resolved (npm fetches a root-bundled or bundle-missing entry from it).

No new error code, export, dependency or file. The prototype measured +23/-4 runtime lines before the header edit. It turned DA6-DA10 green and kept DA1-DA5, DC1-DC5, KI1-KI8 and CY1-CY4 green; the five repository lockfiles (git ls-files '*package-lock.json') admit the same package counts as before (214, 0, 43, 76, 46).
